{
  "id": "apert-syndrome",
  "term": "Apert syndrome",
  "definition": "Apert syndrome is an FGFR-associated craniosynostosis syndrome in which skull sutures close too early, alongside characteristic differences such as fused fingers and toes and other craniofacial changes. In cognition-related contexts, it is noted that cognitive effects can vary across affected individuals.",
